<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n643" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγλαό-καρπος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρπός</span> A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bearing beautiful</i> or <i>goodly fruit</i>, of
			fruit-trees, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοιαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.115
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				11.589
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σικελία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					106
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρήνη</span> Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				274
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>): of Demeter and the Nymphs,
				<i>givers of the fruits of the earth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Cer.
				4
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρπός</span> B) <i>with fair wrists</i>, of
			Thetis, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				3.56
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγλαόκολπος</span>
			).</div>
